From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:00:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: add 802.11s mesh point support

Commit 2ccb8e6ce8a4 ("wifi: rtw88: remove unsupported interface type
of mesh point") removed the mesh point interface type from rtw88. The
mesh code had never been made to work. Parts of the mesh setup are still
in place. A mesh interface gets the AP net type, the beacon function and
a beacon in the reserved page, just like an AP interface. Several pieces
are missing.

mac80211 does not call start_ap and stop_ap for a mesh interface. It
only enables and disables the beacon. The driver therefore never sets
ap_active for mesh, never widens the ATIM window and never runs the
calibration. The reserved page code also gathers the beacon of a mesh
interface before it joins a mesh. mac80211 has no beacon for it at that
point, so the reserved page download fails.

Only port 0 sends beacons. The driver moves an AP interface to port 0,
but it leaves a mesh interface on the port it got.

A mesh peer puts its own address into the BSSID field of its beacons.
The driver sets BIT_CBSSID_BCN after every scan. The hardware then drops
the beacons of the peers. mac80211 needs them to discover peers and to
learn their capabilities. mac80211 sets FIF_OTHER_BSS while a mesh
interface is up. The Realtek vendor driver
clears the BSSID check while a mesh interface is up as well.

The RX path updates the RSSI of a station only for frames that carry
the BSSID of the interface. A mesh interface has no BSSID, so the RSSI
of every peer stays at zero. The firmware rate adaptation and DIG work
with that value.

The security CAM finds group keys only by their key index. Each mesh
peer protects its group frames with its own group key. mac80211 already
handles these peer keys in software, because rtw88 does not support per
station group keys. The group key of the local interface would still
sit in the CAM, and the hardware would apply it to the group frames of
the peers.

Advertise NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT. In the 8822C interface combination
allow a mesh interface in place of the AP interface, so one station and
one AP or mesh interface can run together. Guard that entry with
CONFIG_MAC80211_MESH, because mac80211 removes the mesh type when mesh
support is not built. Run the AP start and stop code when mac80211
enables or disables the beacon of a mesh interface. Treat a mesh
interface like an AP interface for the port switch and the reserved
page. Keep the BSSID check off while FIF_OTHER_BSS is set. Do not turn
it back on at the end of a hardware scan in that case. Match mesh peers
by address when updating the RSSI. Use software crypto for all keys of a
mesh interface.

This makes 802.11s mesh point available on rtw88. A mesh interface and
an AP interface on the same radio are still not possible. The driver
keeps a single beacon in the reserved page and beacons only on port 0.
Chips other than the 8822C have no interface combination, so they get
mesh as their only interface. They were not tested.

Tested on a NanoPi R2S Plus with an RTL8822CS on SDIO at 50 MHz, in an
open mesh with an ath10k peer on channel 36 at 80 MHz. Peering reaches
ESTAB on both sides, also after the peer entry is deleted and after
scans. Ping takes 4 to 7 ms. iperf3 reaches about 60 Mbit/s towards the
board and 31 Mbit/s from it, the same split as in station mode on this
board. Floods of 50 and 200 broadcast frames per second and a 10 minute
soak caused no TX page shortage, no reserved page or beacon download
failure and no lost peering. batman-adv with BATMAN_V runs over the mesh
interface. AP and station mode perform as without this patch.

The analysis and the first draft of this patch and its changelog were
produced in Claude Code sessions with the Claude model claude-opus-5-5.
The same sessions ran the hardware tests. The author reviewed the
change and the results.

Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/fw.c       | 11 +++-
 drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/mac80211.c | 58 +++++++++++++++----
 drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.c     | 12 +++-
 drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/rx.c       |  4 +-
 4 files changed, 67 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/fw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/fw.c
@@ -1576,8 +1576,9 @@ static void rtw_build_rsvd_page_iter(voi
 	struct rtw_vif *rtwvif = (struct rtw_vif *)vif->drv_priv;
 	struct rtw_rsvd_page *rsvd_pkt;
 
-	/* AP not yet started, don't gather its rsvd pages */
-	if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP && !rtwdev->ap_active)
+	/* AP or mesh not yet started, don't gather its rsvd pages */
+	if ((vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP ||
+	     vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT) && !rtwdev->ap_active)
 		return;
 
 	list_for_each_entry(rsvd_pkt, &rtwvif->rsvd_page_list, vif_list) {
@@ -2278,7 +2279,11 @@ void rtw_hw_scan_complete(struct rtw_dev
 	if (!vif)
 		return;
 
-	rtwdev->hal.rcr |= BIT_CBSSID_BCN;
+	/* BIT_AAP is set while mac80211 asks for FIF_OTHER_BSS, which
+	 * a mesh interface does to receive the beacons of its peers.
+	 */
+	if (!(rtwdev->hal.rcr & BIT_AAP))
+		rtwdev->hal.rcr |= BIT_CBSSID_BCN;
 	rtw_write32(rtwdev, REG_RCR, rtwdev->hal.rcr);
 
 	rtw_core_scan_complete(rtwdev, vif, true);
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/mac80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/mac80211.c
@@ -311,6 +311,11 @@ static void rtw_ops_configure_filter(str
 		else
 			rtwdev->hal.rcr |= BIT_CBSSID_BCN;
 	}
+	/* mac80211 sets FIF_OTHER_BSS for mesh. Mesh peers put their own
+	 * address into the BSSID field, so do not filter by BSSID.
+	 */
+	if (*new_flags & FIF_OTHER_BSS)
+		rtwdev->hal.rcr &= ~(BIT_CBSSID_BCN | BIT_CBSSID_DATA);
 
 	rtw_dbg(rtwdev, RTW_DBG_RX,
 		"config rx filter, changed=0x%08x, new=0x%08x, rcr=0x%08x\n",
@@ -369,6 +374,26 @@ static void rtw_conf_tx(struct rtw_dev *
 		__rtw_conf_tx(rtwdev, rtwvif, ac);
 }
 
+static void __rtw_start_ap(struct rtw_dev *rtwdev)
+{
+	const struct rtw_chip_info *chip = rtwdev->chip;
+
+	rtw_write32_set(rtwdev, REG_TCR, BIT_TCR_UPDATE_HGQMD);
+	rtw_write16(rtwdev, REG_ATIMWND, ATIMWND_AP);
+	rtwdev->ap_active = true;
+	rtw_store_op_chan(rtwdev, true);
+	chip->ops->phy_calibration(rtwdev);
+}
+
+static void __rtw_stop_ap(struct rtw_dev *rtwdev)
+{
+	rtw_write32_clr(rtwdev, REG_TCR, BIT_TCR_UPDATE_HGQMD);
+	rtw_write16(rtwdev, REG_ATIMWND, ATIMWND_DEFAULT);
+	rtwdev->ap_active = false;
+	if (!rtw_core_check_sta_active(rtwdev))
+		rtw_clear_op_chan(rtwdev);
+}
+
 static void rtw_ops_bss_info_changed(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 				     struct ieee80211_vif *vif,
 				     struct ieee80211_bss_conf *conf,
@@ -384,6 +409,18 @@ static void rtw_ops_bss_info_changed(str
 
 	rtw_leave_lps_deep(rtwdev);
 
+	/* mac80211 does not call start_ap and stop_ap for mesh. It only
+	 * enables and disables the beacon. Do the AP setup here, before
+	 * the beacon is downloaded below.
+	 */
+	if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT &&
+	    changed & BSS_CHANGED_BEACON_ENABLED) {
+		if (conf->enable_beacon)
+			__rtw_start_ap(rtwdev);
+		else
+			__rtw_stop_ap(rtwdev);
+	}
+
 	if (changed & BSS_CHANGED_ASSOC) {
 		rtw_vif_assoc_changed(rtwvif, conf);
 		if (vif->cfg.assoc) {
@@ -464,14 +501,9 @@ static int rtw_ops_start_ap(struct ieee8
 			    struct ieee80211_bss_conf *link_conf)
 {
 	struct rtw_dev *rtwdev = hw->priv;
-	const struct rtw_chip_info *chip = rtwdev->chip;
 
 	mutex_lock(&rtwdev->mutex);
-	rtw_write32_set(rtwdev, REG_TCR, BIT_TCR_UPDATE_HGQMD);
-	rtw_write16(rtwdev, REG_ATIMWND, ATIMWND_AP);
-	rtwdev->ap_active = true;
-	rtw_store_op_chan(rtwdev, true);
-	chip->ops->phy_calibration(rtwdev);
+	__rtw_start_ap(rtwdev);
 	mutex_unlock(&rtwdev->mutex);
 
 	return 0;
@@ -484,11 +516,7 @@ static void rtw_ops_stop_ap(struct ieee8
 	struct rtw_dev *rtwdev = hw->priv;
 
 	mutex_lock(&rtwdev->mutex);
-	rtw_write32_clr(rtwdev, REG_TCR, BIT_TCR_UPDATE_HGQMD);
-	rtw_write16(rtwdev, REG_ATIMWND, ATIMWND_DEFAULT);
-	rtwdev->ap_active = false;
-	if (!rtw_core_check_sta_active(rtwdev))
-		rtw_clear_op_chan(rtwdev);
+	__rtw_stop_ap(rtwdev);
 	mutex_unlock(&rtwdev->mutex);
 }
 
@@ -560,6 +588,14 @@ static int rtw_ops_set_key(struct ieee80
 	u8 hw_key_idx;
 	int ret = 0;
 
+	/* The CAM finds group keys by key index only. On a mesh
+	 * interface our own group key would be used to decrypt the
+	 * group frames of the peers, which use their own group keys.
+	 * Leave all mesh keys to software crypto.
+	 */
+	if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT)
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+
 	switch (key->cipher) {
 	case WLAN_CIPHER_SUITE_WEP40:
 		hw_key_type = RTW_CAM_WEP40;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/main.c
@@ -111,7 +111,10 @@ static const struct ieee80211_iface_limi
 	},
 	{
 		.max = 1,
-		.types = BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_AP),
+		.types = BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_AP)
+#ifdef CPTCFG_MAC80211_MESH
+			 | BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT)
+#endif
 	}
 };
 
@@ -2285,7 +2288,8 @@ int rtw_register_hw(struct rtw_dev *rtwd
 
 	hw->wiphy->interface_modes = BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION) |
 				     BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_AP) |
-				     BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_ADHOC);
+				     BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_ADHOC) |
+				     BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT);
 	hw->wiphy->available_antennas_tx = hal->antenna_tx;
 	hw->wiphy->available_antennas_rx = hal->antenna_rx;
 
@@ -2431,7 +2435,9 @@ void rtw_core_port_switch(struct rtw_dev
 	struct rtw_vif *rtwvif = (struct rtw_vif *)vif->drv_priv;
 	struct rtw_iter_port_switch_data iter_data;
 
-	if (vif->type != NL80211_IFTYPE_AP || rtwvif->port == RTW_PORT_0)
+	if ((vif->type != NL80211_IFTYPE_AP &&
+	     vif->type != NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT) ||
+	    rtwvif->port == RTW_PORT_0)
 		return;
 
 	iter_data.rtwdev = rtwdev;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/rx.c
@@ -111,7 +111,9 @@ static void rtw_rx_addr_match_iter(void
 	struct rtw_rx_pkt_stat *pkt_stat = iter_data->pkt_stat;
 	u8 *bssid = iter_data->bssid;
 
-	if (!ether_addr_equal(vif->bss_conf.bssid, bssid))
+	/* A mesh interface has no BSSID. Match its peers by address. */
+	if (vif->type != NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT &&
+	    !ether_addr_equal(vif->bss_conf.bssid, bssid))
 		return;
 
 	if (!(ether_addr_equal(vif->addr, hdr->addr1) ||
